{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1492527-question-about-a-character-concept","id":1492527,"title":"Question about a Character Concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-07T10:09:16-07:00","id":1492527,"title":"Question about a Character Concept","content":"I'm working on a character concept, it is &quot;The Butler&quot;<br /> <br /> The Boggan must be the the most obvious option, however this kith just don't really meet my aesthetic tastes.<br /> So I were wondering if the Autumn Shide kith can fit to this concept as well (maybe as chief servant).<br /> What's your opinion on this silly question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T11:26:12-07:00","id":1492538,"title":"","content":"I don't see why an Autumn Sidhe would not make for an excellent butler. A proper butler is like a lord among a households staff. See Angus Hudson from the British soap opera Upstairs Downstairs for an example. Hudson was smart, charming, an inspiring leader, and thoroughly IN CHARGE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T11:28:04-07:00","id":1492539,"title":"","content":"It is perfectly doable. Even an Arcadian Sidhe could have been relegated to such a role depending on circumstances and bad luck, but any other Kith, including Autumn Sidhe, could end up at this job and decide to fully embrace it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you could also have a Boggan that isn't very like the Kith's standards. But given the idea of a buttler, I think Boggan wouldn't necessarily fit anyway, and Sidhe may be a good choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T12:33:29-07:00","id":1492546,"title":"","content":"Butlers and Maids were sometimes from minor noble houses especially those children that didn't have anything to inherit. While peasants where used for a lot of the normal household work (cooking, yardwork, etc.) a Great house wouldn't want something that common to attend them.<br /> <br /> I can see Fae Nobles taking on the same kind of stance. While Boggans are the staff, you wouldn't want one to be your attendant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T13:59:49-07:00","id":1492556,"title":"","content":"The female version of the <i>Butler</i> is the <i>Housekeeper</i>. Both are more than just personal servants, but the most trusted ones, whose duties require care, skill, social acumen and frequently management and leading skills. The precise duties vary from household to household, but in big ones they're usually chief of staff and specially responsible for organizing work that will happen in front of guests (like serving the food) or deal with valuable assets (like cleaning fragile decoration), although their duties can go well beyond, and sometimes you may even have an entire team of them with specialized areas of responsibility and a chief butler/housekeeper.<br /> <br /> Originally they served wine and other beverages to their masters, this job being executed by the most trusted servants or slaves because those beverages were expensive and of hard maintenance, and their vessels more fragile than modern glass bottles, so accidents would waste a lot of resources.<br /> <br /> All in all, that's the kind of job that could be executed by any kith based on the household and its needs. Depending on the household it could even require Title 1 all by itself. Of course, that would be a very specific case, but the truth is, when butlers are concerned every case is unique, even the less expensive ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T06:49:30-07:00","id":1493058,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys and girls!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}